  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed at the Republic in New Orleans, Louisiana, on Monday, November 3, 2008 [1][2]. This event is the 130th of 467 archived shows for the band, following a performance at the Wonder Ballroom on October 21, 2008 [2]. The recommended recording is a 16-bit FLAC file containing 19 songs with a total duration of 84 minutes [1]. The audio was taped and transferred by ezralite23 [1]. The setlist opens with “Have to Explode” and “Heretic Pride” before moving into “Slow West Vultures” and “Moon Over Goldsboro” [1]. “Collapsing Stars” is the first in the archive, with only eight archived performances, while “Here I Am” is mythic rare with just two archived performances [1]. “Thank You Mario But Our Princess Is In Another Castle” is also first in the archive [1]. Later tracks include “Mosquito Repellent,” “Suedehead,” and “Supergenesis,” all of which are rare with six, five, and six archived performances respectively [1]. The set concludes with “Sept 15th 1983,” “No Children,” “See America Right,” “This Year,” “Houseguest,” and “Going to Georgia” [1]. The uploader notes the recording is crisp and clear overall, though typical audience noise is present [1]. An encore features John solo acoustic with Kaki King on co-vocals and guitar [1].",
